    "QSPI": {
      "protocol": "1-bit SPI NAND via SPIM3 on dedicated QSPI pins (or hybrid QSPI READOC=0x03)",
      "clock_hz": 8000000,
      "max_clock_hz": 8000000,
      "voltage_v": 1.8,
      "silicon_instance": "SPIM3",
      "peripheral_id": 12,
      "base_address": "0x4000C000",
      "silicon_note": "Retains contract bus key 'QSPI' for 1-to-1 INTERFACE_CONTRACT.json parity. On nRF5340 silicon, QSPI.CINSTRCONF executes strictly on a single data line (IO0/IO1, <= 8 payload bytes) and QSPI EasyDMA READ4O/PP4O hard-codes 24-bit addresses vs W25N01JW's 16-bit column address. Furthermore, nRF5340 SPIM0..SPIM3 are hardware-capped at 8 MHz max SCLK (only SPIM4 supports higher SCLK rates). Therefore M3 firmware drives W25N01JW over the dedicated P0.13..P0.18 pins using SPIM3 (Peripheral ID 12, 0x4000C000, 8 MHz / 8 Mbps / ~1.0 MB/s wire rate 1-bit SPI NAND mode with P0.13=MOSI/SI, P0.14=MISO/SO, P0.15=/WP held 1V8, P0.16=/HOLD held 1V8, P0.17=SCK, P0.18=FLASH_CS_N), which easily sustains 8,044 B/s logging and 650 KB/s USB FS read offload and has zero ID conflict with TWIM0(8), SPIM1(9), SPIM4(10), or TWIM2(11) — or alternatively hybrid QSPI (CINSTRCONF for control + READOC=READ 0x03 1-bit 24-bit [16b CA + 8b dummy]) as an optional faster read alternative.",
      "pins": {
        "IO0": { "pin": "P0.13", "ball": "AL5", "drive": "H0H1", "spim3_role": "MOSI / SI" },
        "IO1": { "pin": "P0.14", "ball": "AK8", "drive": "H0H1", "spim3_role": "MISO / SO" },
        "IO2": { "pin": "P0.15", "ball": "AK10", "drive": "H0H1", "spim3_role": "/WP (driven HIGH 1V8 in 1-bit SPI)" },
        "IO3": { "pin": "P0.16", "ball": "AL9", "drive": "H0H1", "spim3_role": "/HOLD (driven HIGH 1V8 in 1-bit SPI)" },
        "SCK": { "pin": "P0.17", "ball": "AK12", "drive": "H0H1", "spim3_role": "SCK" },
        "FLASH_CS_N": { "pin": "P0.18", "ball": "AK14", "drive": "H0H1", "pullup_ohms": 10000, "spim3_role": "CS_N" }
      },
      "devices": [
        {
          "part_number": "W25N01JW",
          "full_part_number": "W25N01JWZEIG",
          "capacity_mb": 128,
          "page_bytes": 2048,
          "block_bytes": 131072,
          "usable_ring_blocks": 998
        }
      ]
    },
